Title: Judge's New X Word Puzzle No. 1
Author: Homer M. Parsons

ITCH#STRAP#PICK
N#LABOR#NAKED#I
KNOW#LEMON#TEST
YET#S#MAN#C#ATE
#W#CABOT#HAM#A#
SER#CARRION#ALA
PLUG#R#I#NOOSES
A#MERRYMAKERS#P
DROMIO#O#I#BABE
EAR#MORNING#YEN
#I#HEM#INGOT#N#
USE#S#CAT#B#ICE
TELL#SALAD#ACHE
A#SILOS#CONGO#L
HEED#STATE#ENDS

A1. What is it that makes people come to the scratch? ~ ITCH
A4. What article is considered effective in persuading youth to righteousness? ~ STRAP
A8. What do gold-digger's dig with? ~ PICK
A11. What do workmen do when the boss comes around? ~ LABOR
A12. What was Godiva? ~ NAKED
A13. What word is pronounced like a negative; but means "understand"? ~ KNOW
A15. What fruit-name is applied to a person of acid disposition? ~ LEMON
A17. What is more difficult for a speedy college boy to pass than a high-powered roadster? ~ TEST
A19. What conjunction means "nevertheless"? ~ YET
A21. At what study is a Vassar student most proficient? ~ MAN
A23. What did Adam do which caused all the trouble? ~ ATE
A24. What was the surname of the English navigators—father and son—who discovered the American continent in 1497? ~ CABOT
A26. What is a bad actor? ~ HAM
A27. What is the abbreviation for something Emerson said could be found in stones? ~ SER
A29. What is many an old buzzard looking for? ~ CARRION
A30. What is an abbreviation for a popular Mammy state? ~ ALA
A32. What is there in common about the following: a slow horse, an electric socket, a stiff hat and a square of chewing tobacco? ~ PLUG
A34. What kind of neckties are very unpopular? ~ NOOSES
A36. What are night clubs inhabited by—before the checks come around? ~ MERRYMAKERS
A38. Name twin brothers in Shakespeare's Comedy of Errors who were often taken for one another. ~ DROMIO
A40. Who runs right home after the ball is over? ~ BABE
A42. Name a listening-in device. ~ EAR
A43. What is it in New York when it's 2 P. M. in London? ~ MORNING
A46. What does 100 sen equal in Tokio? ~ YEN
A47. What part of a girl's dress is considerably above two feet? ~ HEM
A48. What would you call a mass of cast metal from a mold? ~ INGOT
A49. Name a word which means "employment to an end." ~ USE
A51. What makes a good rat trap? ~ CAT
A52. In what form could water be termed "hard drink"? ~ ICE
A54. What are daisies not supposed to do? ~ TELL
A56. What part of a dinner is usually served uncooked? ~ SALAD
A58. What is a pain in the neck? ~ ACHE
A59. In what is green fodder packed——? ~ SILOS
A60. What is a negro who comes from the Kongo section of Africa called? ~ CONGO
A61. What is it to take notice? ~ HEED
A62. What is Washington? (The right answer will fit.) ~ STATE
A63. What is supposed to meet with a hoop snake? ~ ENDS

D1. What adjective means "very, very black"? ~ INKY
D2. What is a coagulum? ~ CLOT
D3. What is the opposite of "gee"? ~ HAW
D4. What causes freckles? ~ SOL
D5. What does an editor in California call a quake? ~ TREMOR
D6. Who writes the jokes credited to exchange? ~ ANON
D7. What can George Jean Nathan proficiently do to a bum show? ~ PAN
D8. What do flappers love to do? ~ PET
D9. What is useless unless it's executed? ~ IDEA
D10. Name one kind of high flyer. ~ KITE
D14. From what kind of post do winding stairs radiate? ~ NEWEL
D16. What kind of difficulties do married people get into? ~ MATRIMONIAL
D18. What kind of jokes do you hear in most vaudeville shows? ~ STALE
D20. Name one of certain tribe of Algonquin Indians. ~ SAC
D22. What should never be tipped? ~ CANOE
D25. In what place do mortals come in contact with the spirit world? ~ BARROOM
D26. By what is a goose in a Ford recognized? ~ HONKING
D27. What is good for a quick turnover? ~ SPADE
D28. What is apt to fly around in sewing circles? ~ RUMOR
D30. What does a handsome young chemist do for a gold-digger? ~ ASSAY
D31. What is a famous quaker? ~ ASPEN
D33. What is often an engaging symbol? ~ GEM
D35. Name a heavenly body. (Not Gilda Gray's.) ~ ORB
D37. What is usually found in poetry? (This must be spelled in the older and more etymologically correct manner.) ~ RIMES
D39. Can you name an uplifting verb? ~ RAISE
D41. What have the following in common: harness-makers, second-rate ball players and judges? ~ BENCH
D44. In what condition is it impossible to keep a bank roll? ~ INTACT
D45. Can you name one thing recently exported to China? ~ GOB
D49. In what state is a Jew considered a Gentile? ~ UTAH
D50. What conjunction means "otherwise"? ~ ELSE
D51. What are bad actors often found in? ~ CAST
D52. Can you give the name of one sacred image? ~ ICON
D53. What kind of fish look like snakes? ~ EELS
D55. What is it that is always going over the top? ~ LID
D56. Give a well known signal of distress. ~ SOS
D57. What is always a little deer? ~ DOE
D58. What is one secret any woman can keep? ~ AGE
